WEBVTT

00:00:00.707 --> 00:00:01.400
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:02.338 --> 00:00:03.055
a

00:00:03.892 --> 00:00:05.074
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> It’s a verb.

00:00:05.631 --> 00:00:07.958
It’s the opposite of <i>lose</i>.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.064
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> b

00:00:10.913 --> 00:00:12.321
<v><b>Speaker B:</b></v> It’s something you drink.

00:00:12.817 --> 00:00:17.080
It’s alcoholic and it can be red, white, or rosé.

00:00:19.066 --> 00:00:19.726
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.279
a

00:00:22.337 --> 00:00:28.114
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> It’s an animal which people have in their house, for example a cat.

00:00:29.555 --> 00:00:30.243
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> b

00:00:31.121 --> 00:00:33.869
<v><b>Speaker B:</b></v> It’s the short form of the name <i>Peter</i>.

00:00:35.798 --> 00:00:36.630
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:37.564 --> 00:00:38.268
a

00:00:39.151 --> 00:00:42.428
<v><b>Speaker A:</b></v> It’s an adjective similar to <i>crazy</i>.

00:00:43.895 --> 00:00:44.548
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> b

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:48.452
<v><b>Speaker B:</b></v> It’s the past tense of the verb <i>make</i>.